{"parentUuid":"2b380bbf-0782-45da-9654-fc03c7dd085d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DTJWBwo4186wc3t5WhbyUA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good catch — this is a real edge case. Walking through it:\n\n**Ctrl+C:**\n- The process is SIGKILL'd (or SIGINT'd into a hard exit). No `SessionEnd` hook fires.\n- The kernel auto-releases the `flock` when the FD closes on exit, so the lock isn't stuck. The lock *file* on disk persists but is unlocked — fine, next acquirer reuses it.\n- The `<sid>.agent` hint, `<sid>.json` state, and `<sid>.lock` file all persist. Nothing cleans them up — `ClearSessionState` is only called from `entire doctor` cleanup, never from `SessionEnd` (`lifecycle.go:642-679` just marks ENDED, doesn't clear).\n\n**`claude -c`** (which reuses the same session_id and the same transcript JSONL):\n\n1. SessionStart fires.\n2. `StoreAgentTypeHint` runs `O_CREATE|O_EXCL` on `<sid>.agent` → file already exists → returns `(created=false, err=nil)`.\n3. `claimedFirst = false`.\n4. **Banner is suppressed.**\n5. TurnStart fires → state file already exists → goes through the \"session already exists\" branch → `correctSessionAgentType` runs against the transcript path → AgentType stays correct.\n\nFunctionally everything still works (agent attribution is preserved, the lock cycles cleanly, checkpoints continue), but the user does *not* see the \"Entire CLI will link this conversation…\" banner on the resumed run. That's a behavioral change from before this PR, where the banner was always emitted on every SessionStart.\n\nWhether that's a bug depends on intent:\n\n- **The dedup test** (`TestHandleLifecycleSessionStart_GeminiRepeatSourceDoesNotDuplicate`) is explicitly about *one process* firing SessionStart multiple times in a single run. `claude -c` is a *new process* — arguably the user expects the banner again to confirm Entire is still tracking.\n- **The hint mechanism** treats \"session_id\" as a stable identity. If you accept that, suppressing on resume is consistent.\n\nIf you want the banner to come back on `claude -c`, the cleanest fix is to differentiate the SessionStart `source` payload — Claude Code sends `source: \"resume\"` (or `\"startup\"`/`\"clear\"`/`\"compact\"`) — and force `claimedFirst = true` when source ≠ `\"startup\"`. The hint check still suppresses the cross-agent forwarded duplicate (Cursor → Claude), because that fires with `source: \"startup\"` from both. Gemini's repeat fires both as the same agent in one process, so it's already covered.\n\nSame logic applies to a Cursor session resumed with `cursor-agent --resume <id>` — the `.agent` hint persists and the banner is suppressed.\n\nWorth deciding before merge. My read is the resume case probably wants the banner, but it's a judgment call."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1467,"cache_read_input_tokens":155278,"output_tokens":1124,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":155278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaZz7NqrAhKuaPJ3K8ZU5","type":"assistant","uuid":"475eccc8-dd74-469c-8af2-24af6d5a7fdf","timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:51:24.133Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c3eb3dfd-f856-4fb0-901f-7bae4034e1d7","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"ashtom/cursor-fix"}
